Cell[TextData[{
 "A special propagator of a cochain complex with a pairing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["d",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
      RowBox[{"-", ",", "-"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}]}], ")"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ed398c2-3ddd-499b-9e67-d698a501e1ef"],
 " is a linear map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], ":", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ccd4285e-75c9-4647-bc34-def585976b91"],
 " of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4a29e87-a8c9-4a3c-8819-71df581a97d8"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13a0e644-be8b-4b70-826d-71c7a47c4504"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
    StyleBox["P", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c07a1c0-3848-4aa6-a87b-cc036faf1e31"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c70b86a-72c9-4f83-a127-29ac46f608fa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]},
      "Abs"]], 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e1458a9b-b3ce-4b64-9246-71cf0a9b182a"],
 " (arXiv:2004.07362, Definition 3.16)."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.10.01: Design review - built in HodgeDecompositions H5 from the \
blueprint of H4, whose ten choices Pavel kept in H4a. The propagator is \
computed once and applied many times, so it is an inert object that applies \
to an element as a LinearSolveFunction does, p[e]; SpecialPropagator[e, \
decomposition], computing P again for each element, was the alternative. The \
object carries the decomposition it came from, as a decomposition carries its \
complex, so its relations are those of the propagator followed by those of \
the decomposition; carrying only the complex, from which \
FindHodgeDecomposition[p] recovers the decomposition, was the alternative. \
The four relations of Definition 3.16 are conditions on the operator in every \
degree, so they have arity 0 and Obstruction lists the degrees where they \
fail, as for the axioms of a decomposition; identities on one and on two \
elements, arities 1, 1, 1 and 2 as for a complex, were the alternative. There \
is no SpecialPropagatorQ: RelationsQ tests the relations. A pre-Hodge \
decomposition gives a special homotopy operator without the symmetry \
(arXiv:2004.07362, Remark 4.2), not a propagator, so SpecialPropagator of one \
returns unevaluated. A decomposition whose parts are not a basis in some \
degree has no propagator and returns unevaluated as well; data whose images \
miss a basis element, or send an element of degree k outside the span of the \
basis of degree k - 1, is not a propagator, and Relations, Obstruction, \
RelationsQ and the application return unevaluated on it. The images are found \
by one inverse matrix per degree, of the frame of the decomposition in the \
basis. Prior art: the Wolfram Language has no homotopy operators of a cochain \
complex. In homological perturbation theory P is the homotopy of a special \
deformation retract onto the harmonic subspace, with the side conditions hh = \
0, hi = 0 and ph = 0, which are P^2 = 0 and P pi = pi P = 0; the symmetry \
with respect to the pairing is what a propagator adds. The engine of the \
verification suites has no counterpart.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
